 =?UTF-8?q?=20on=20the=20lock=20screen?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On phones the lock screen shows the newest notifications as cards in
the language of the receipt (export/mockups 01_lock): the app icon in a
keycap frame, "App · time", the title and two lines of text, as many
cards as fit (at most three) and "+ N další oznámení" for the rest. The
cards read the same list as the notification stack (after the lock
screen filters) and redact sensitive notifications like the receipt; a
tap opens the notification through the bouncer when the device is
locked. They hide while dozing (AOD keeps its icon shelf) and move with
the burn-in offset. The notification stack stays with no height for
its lifecycle (heads-up, clear all, shelf), like in the notification
shade.

BudikNotificationActions becomes a SysUI singleton shared by the shade
and the lock screen (one icon cache).
